-orpheum-theatre-opened-in-1922-and-later-faced-decades-of-preservation-battles-after-a-15-month-closure-the-landmark-has-reopened-following-a-13-million-restoration-project/articleshow/134890849.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T03:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134890913,imgsize-811301.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[David Baldacci’s Feeding Body &amp; Mind initiative distributes over 1 million books through food banks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134890819.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[David and Michelle Baldacci launched Feeding Body &amp; Mind as a dual initiative to tackle food insecurity and improve literacy rates. This program gathers and disperses books through local food banks, allowing over a million families the opportunity to take home reading materials. By linking food support with literacy resources, it empowers families to enhance their reading skills and underscores the critical need for accessible literature in challenging times.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/author-david-baldacci-helped-turn-food-banks-into-places-where-families-could-also-find-books-his-feeding-body-mind-initiative-has-collected-and-distributed-more-than-1-million-books/articleshow/134890819.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/author-david-baldacci-helped-turn-food-banks-into-places-where-families-could-also-find-books-his-feeding-body-mind-initiative-has-collected-and-distributed-more-than-1-million-books/articleshow/134890819.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T03:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134891034,imgsize-51653.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2026 Hit The Bricks Fundraiser: Wake Forest relay sets records; cancer fund tops $2.1 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134883620.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a display of community spirit, Wake Forest University successfully hosted its Hit the Bricks fundraiser on October 1, bringing together 2,406 participants and raising an impressive nearly $407,000. This year marked a significant increase in both participation and funds compared to last year. Celebrating 23 years, Hit the Bricks has now raised over $2.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wake-forests-student-run-hit-the-bricks-drew-2406-runners-and-walkers-for-11862-laps-and-raised-nearly-407000-in-one-day-beating-last-years-record-and-pushing-the-event-past-2-1-million/articleshow/134883620.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wake-forests-student-run-hit-the-bricks-drew-2406-runners-and-walkers-for-11862-laps-and-raised-nearly-407000-in-one-day-beating-last-years-record-and-pushing-the-event-past-2-1-million/articleshow/134883620.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T03:49:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134883659,imgsize-2007025.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Council Drops 6,752 Homes: Hertsmere rewrites Local Plan; consultation continues]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134885690.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Hertsmere Borough Council has decided to withdraw multiple large housing projects based on community feedback from public consultations. The updated Local Plan still aims to provide over 14,000 homes, focusing on urban areas. This action showcases the balance between housing demand and the necessity for appropriate infrastructure. Although four major developments have been removed, the overall housing strategy remains effective.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-hertfordshire-plan-proposed-3750-homes-at-well-end-but-after-public-consultation-the-council-dropped-the-entire-extension-as-part-of-a-wider-removal-of-6752-planned-homes-from-its-local-plan/articleshow/134885690.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-hertfordshire-plan-proposed-3750-homes-at-well-end-but-after-public-consultation-the-council-dropped-the-entire-extension-as-part-of-a-wider-removal-of-6752-planned-homes-from-its-local-plan/articleshow/134885690.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T02:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134885733,imgsize-1308377.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bus Driver Removal Dispute: Kitten rescue costs Maryland driver route; parents press for return]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134883555.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Cynthia Morgan, a dedicated school bus driver in Maryland, was dismissed after she permitted a student to save a kitten. This decision has ignited discussions on student welfare and the appropriateness of the response. Parents and locals are rallying for her return as support grows. The school district insists on safety protocols, reflecting on Morgan's history with students, prompting an evaluation of transport safety rules and disciplinary actions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-67-year-old-maryland-school-bus-driver-was-removed-from-her-route-after-allowing-a-10-year-old-boy-to-step-off-and-rescue-a-kitten-a-petition-seeking-her-reinstatement-have-800-plus-signatures/articleshow/134883555.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-67-year-old-maryland-school-bus-driver-was-removed-from-her-route-after-allowing-a-10-year-old-boy-to-step-off-and-rescue-a-kitten-a-petition-seeking-her-reinstatement-have-800-plus-signatures/articleshow/134883555.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T01:54:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134883590,imgsize-1520162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Julia Child’s Provence home is now a cooking school where guests use her original kitchen]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134883400.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[La Pitchoune, once the famed kitchen of Julia Child, remains a vibrant hub for culinary enthusiasts. Over the years, it has transformed into an enchanting cooking school and vacation rental, inviting guests to recreate Julia's beloved dishes. The Held family, who took over in 2016, have ensured that the legacy and authentic charm of the kitchen endures, inspiring visitors to embrace the culinary arts with Julia's spirit guiding their hands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/julia-child-and-her-husband-built-la-pitchoune-in-provence-in-1963-and-used-it-for-nearly-three-decades-after-she-gave-it-up-in-1992-the-home-became-a-cooking-school-where-guests-still-cook-in-her-original-kitchen/articleshow/134883400.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/julia-child-and-her-husband-built-la-pitchoune-in-provence-in-1963-and-used-it-for-nearly-three-decades-after-she-gave-it-up-in-1992-the-home-became-a-cooking-school-where-guests-still-cook-in-her-original-kitchen/articleshow/134883400.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T00:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134883529,imgsize-203002.cms"/></item></channel></rss>